# All build and test artifacts (compiled binaries, images, captures, logs,
# diagnostic dumps) live under build/ -- rebuild/reproduce via the Makefile
# or `make deploy` instead of committing any of it.
build/

# Large diagnostic dumps / captured test sessions -- useful for a specific
# debugging session, not for the repo (can be multi-MB to multi-GB). Not
# just a build/ subset: tools/captures/ (kept locally, not git-tracked)
# also holds these.
#
# Exceptions: small, purpose-built regression fixtures ARE committed --
# tools/captures/resolution-change-gap-repro.cap (a 1s trim, see
# tools/trim-capture.py) and tools/captures/trimmed/*.cap (10s trims of
# the full local corpus, consumed by tools/pytest/test_render_health.py).
# Both are generic enough to be meaningful without the original session's
# full-length capture, small enough to commit as regular blobs (see
# image-builder/vendored-debs/ for the project's own precedent on that
# size threshold), and required for those tests to run at all outside
# this machine.
*.cap
!tools/captures/resolution-change-gap-repro.cap
!tools/captures/trimmed/*.cap
*.h264
planes.txt

# Full DietPi disk image -- 1GB+, embeds this network's WiFi credentials,
# and isn't the reproducible artifact (see README.md "Known gaps" #2)
*.img

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Personal, machine-specific build settings (WiFi credentials, overscan
# tuning, anything else personal added later) -- read by `make image` if
# present, entirely optional otherwise. See personal.env.example for the
# format. Never commit real values.
/personal.env

# tools/pytest/'s project-local venv (tools/pytest-setup.sh) and bytecode
# cache -- rebuildable, machine-specific, not source.
tools/pytest/.venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/

# Claude Code session-local state: machine-specific permission overrides and
# agent worktrees. The shared parts (CLAUDE.md, .claude/agents/) are committed.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/

# JetBrains IDEs
.idea/
